A short opening paragraph in the first column.

|

A much longer second column. Without an explicit column break the
auto-balancer would split this content roughly evenly across both
columns; the leading `|` forces the break so the first column stays
short and everything from here on flows into the second column.

The second paragraph keeps going to give the renderer enough text to
demonstrate that wrapping happens inside the second column, not back
across into the first.

A third paragraph for good measure — short columns on the left, a tall
stack on the right.
